  "details": "There's an issue currently that I'm facing with my gameworld and it's with VRCStation. When a player changes their avatar while they are in the VRCStation it kicks them off for a bit.\n\nI'm not sure if this is the default behavior however I'm pretty sure before this wasn't the case.\n\nHere's how I configured my VRCStation:\n\n- Player Mobility: Immobilize\n\n- Disable Station Exit\n\n- Can Use Station From Station\n\n- Has Animator Controller.\n\nSteps to Produce:\n\n1. Put a player in a VRCStation (Usinig code U#)\n\n2. Change Avatar\n\n3. Player can move while avatar is loading.\n\n4. Player returns to the VRCStation after the avatar is loaded (This is VRC Default Behavior)\n\nOther issues noted:\n\n1. it seems like when the avatar is still loading and the other players is able to load your avatar first, for them you're stuck in the VRCStation until you fully loaded your avatar in your side. Sometimes this causes desync where people will see you stuck in that station.\n\nI think the fix is here is that player shouldn't return to the VRCStation after the avatar is loaded. But im not sure how to bandaid this.",
